1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:06,528
You cheating bastard!

2
00:00:06,611 --> 00:00:07,445
What?

3
00:00:07,529 --> 00:00:10,698
You're the worst! Apologize to your wife!

4
00:00:10,782 --> 00:00:12,116
I didn't do it.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,368
<i>I did not have an affair.</i>

6
00:00:13,451 --> 00:00:15,829
<i>That article is a complete lie.</i>

7
00:00:17,997 --> 00:00:19,249
Jin Ichijo.

8
00:00:19,332 --> 00:00:21,543
Surrounded by young girls
on a harem vacation

9
00:00:21,626 --> 00:00:23,336
in the middle of a major scandal…

10
00:00:26,548 --> 00:00:27,757
Are you leaving already?

11
00:00:27,841 --> 00:00:30,635
<i>Something has been bothering me.</i>

12
00:00:30,718 --> 00:00:31,761
Enough!

13
00:00:31,845 --> 00:00:34,013
Stop looking at the Internet.

14
00:00:35,098 --> 00:00:36,057
It's so delicious.

15
00:00:36,141 --> 00:00:37,225
Shall we drink?

16
00:00:37,308 --> 00:00:40,603
Vacation is the best!

17
00:00:41,271 --> 00:00:42,897
Just how angry is your wife?

18
00:00:42,981 --> 00:00:45,859
A scorned woman's revenge is terrifying.

19
00:00:46,526 --> 00:00:47,569
What? Who is it?

20
00:00:48,236 --> 00:00:49,946
Who is it?!

21
00:00:51,656 --> 00:00:52,866
Who might you be?

22
00:00:53,449 --> 00:00:54,534
I am…

23
00:00:55,034 --> 00:00:56,911
Jin Ichijo's wife.

24
00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:00,290
Is…

25
00:01:00,915 --> 00:01:02,542
my husband here?

26
00:01:07,714 --> 00:01:08,590
All set.

27
00:01:13,928 --> 00:01:15,722
Here you go.

28
00:01:23,897 --> 00:01:25,857
To think his wife would come here…

29
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,483
How did she even find this place?

30
00:01:27,567 --> 00:01:29,235
Maybe she put a GPS tracker on him?

31
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:32,864
What? You mean he was cheating
all over with a GPS attached to him?

32
00:01:32,947 --> 00:01:35,116
Old-school actors are like that,
didn't you know?

33
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:36,618
What are we going to do?

34
00:01:36,701 --> 00:01:38,828
This will be a bloodbath.

35
00:01:47,754 --> 00:01:51,382
This is a compote made from
the summer oranges in our garden.

36
00:01:52,467 --> 00:01:53,927
Please try it.

37
00:01:57,222 --> 00:01:58,932
Midori, when did you make this?

38
00:01:59,015 --> 00:02:01,142
I think I made it yesterday while drunk.

39
00:02:01,226 --> 00:02:02,352
I don't really remember.

40
00:02:22,997 --> 00:02:24,165
It's good.

41
00:02:27,877 --> 00:02:30,505
So you can pick summer oranges
in the garden…

42
00:02:31,881 --> 00:02:33,883
What a wonderful villa.

43
00:02:34,592 --> 00:02:36,135
Thank you.

44
00:02:36,219 --> 00:02:39,180
This villa was left behind
by my grandmother.

45
00:02:39,264 --> 00:02:42,767
We thought we could spend the summer here.

46
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:45,812
That's right. We all happen to be
unemployed right now.

47
00:02:45,895 --> 00:02:48,815
It's what you would call
a vacation from life!

48
00:02:50,566 --> 00:02:52,026
Vacation…

49
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:57,240
You too. You came here…

50
00:02:59,784 --> 00:03:02,120
to take a vacation, didn't you?

51
00:03:04,288 --> 00:03:06,916
No, it's not like that.

52
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,129
I just wanted to escape from the media.

53
00:03:33,735 --> 00:03:35,820
What are you trying to do?

54
00:03:39,115 --> 00:03:43,244
Human issues have nothing
to do with us, right?

55
00:03:44,078 --> 00:03:45,538
Sea God.

56
00:03:47,373 --> 00:03:49,917
SEA GOD

57
00:03:50,001 --> 00:03:53,463
It's best not to stick your nose
into human affairs.

58
00:03:54,005 --> 00:03:55,214
You…

59
00:03:56,007 --> 00:04:00,178
do you know who that man really is?

60
00:04:03,014 --> 00:04:04,849
Weekly Shuubun<i>.</i>

61
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:09,729
A magazine that makes money
week after week off celebrity scandals.

62
00:04:11,314 --> 00:04:14,692
Humans all have secrets, after all.

63
00:04:14,776 --> 00:04:17,820
They expose those secrets
to make a profit.

64
00:04:17,904 --> 00:04:21,991
Sometimes, they even end up
taking people's lives.

65
00:04:22,742 --> 00:04:24,786
They're basically like demons.

66
00:04:25,661 --> 00:04:28,998
Though, saying that
to a Grim Reaper is a bit strange.

67
00:04:32,794 --> 00:04:33,795
Yes.

68
00:05:10,748 --> 00:05:11,833
Ryoko.

69
00:05:12,708 --> 00:05:16,295
I have truly caused you so much trouble.

70
00:05:16,379 --> 00:05:17,755
I'm at your mercy!

71
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:19,298
I am so sorry!

72
00:05:19,382 --> 00:05:20,258
He's groveling!

73
00:05:20,341 --> 00:05:23,261
The poor wife! This is just too painful.

74
00:05:23,344 --> 00:05:26,055
If it's come to this, she should just get
a big payout and divorce him.

75
00:05:26,139 --> 00:05:27,348
The wife is crying.

76
00:05:27,432 --> 00:05:29,183
This situation is terrible.

77
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:30,184
Konta.

78
00:05:30,268 --> 00:05:32,353
-What?
-Are we doing a barbecue tonight?

79
00:05:32,437 --> 00:05:34,397
-Will his wife want some?
-Are you stupid?

80
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:38,151
This is no time for that! As Rinrin said,
a scorned woman's revenge is terrifying!

81
00:05:38,234 --> 00:05:40,278
Mr. Jin may just get stabbed!

82
00:05:40,361 --> 00:05:43,114
-Maybe we should hide the kitchen knives.
-Maybe.

83
00:05:44,115 --> 00:05:45,408
I…

84
00:05:45,491 --> 00:05:47,535
I'm so ashamed.

85
00:05:47,618 --> 00:05:51,330
At this age, to be humiliated like this…

86
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:54,625
This is hell.

87
00:05:56,043 --> 00:05:57,712
A living hell!

88
00:05:58,212 --> 00:05:59,380
I'm at fault.

89
00:06:00,006 --> 00:06:01,632
I am at your mercy!

90
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:07,471
I didn't think I would be caught
by <i>Shuubun</i>, hugging on the street.

91
00:06:09,599 --> 00:06:11,017
And it wasn't…

92
00:06:13,144 --> 00:06:14,437
just once, you know!

93
00:06:16,647 --> 00:06:17,607
It was three times!

94
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:18,608
That hurts.

95
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,526
Three times!

96
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:22,236
Why didn't you notice?

97
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,989
Your guard was way too low! Idiot!

98
00:06:25,072 --> 00:06:27,950
Ryoko, I am at your mercy!

99
00:06:28,034 --> 00:06:29,327
I am so sorry!

100
00:06:31,204 --> 00:06:31,954
Idiot.

101
00:06:32,747 --> 00:06:33,915
Idiot!

102
00:06:37,001 --> 00:06:38,211
-Idiot!
-I'm sorry!

103
00:06:38,294 --> 00:06:41,672
-Idiot! Don't run!
-I'm sorry!

104
00:06:41,756 --> 00:06:43,090
What should we do?

105
00:06:43,174 --> 00:06:44,592
Let's hide the knives!

106
00:06:44,675 --> 00:06:46,928
Let's hide everything
that could be used as a weapon.

107
00:06:47,011 --> 00:06:48,262
Hide them! What is there?

108
00:06:49,263 --> 00:06:50,514
Should we hide this too?

109
00:06:51,849 --> 00:06:54,769
Hey! You look like a serial killer!

110
00:06:54,852 --> 00:06:57,146
The wife might have brought
a weapon with her.

111
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:59,941
-Let's take away her bag!
-The bag!

112
00:07:00,024 --> 00:07:01,525
You absolute fool!

113
00:07:02,652 --> 00:07:03,736
Idiot!

114
00:07:03,819 --> 00:07:06,280
You! You absolute idiot!

115
00:07:06,364 --> 00:07:08,032
Okay!

116
00:07:08,115 --> 00:07:09,951
Idiot!

117
00:07:13,621 --> 00:07:15,289
-Check if there's a weapon inside!
-Yes!

118
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:17,625
Okay!

119
00:07:21,587 --> 00:07:22,588
What is this?

120
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:25,591
Yes.

121
00:07:25,675 --> 00:07:28,761
The second article
will be a hit with this, Chief Editor.

122
00:07:28,844 --> 00:07:31,889
The cheating piece of trash
Jin Ichijo shows no remorse!

123
00:07:31,973 --> 00:07:35,101
Gathering <i>gyaru </i>at a Tatsumi Town villa
for a harem drinking party!

124
00:07:36,102 --> 00:07:39,021
Let's hit him hard this week too!

125
00:07:39,105 --> 00:07:41,315
Let's keep the fire going!

126
00:07:43,568 --> 00:07:46,112
-Do you enjoy lighting fires?
-Whoa!

127
00:07:46,195 --> 00:07:47,530
What the hell?

128
00:07:48,614 --> 00:07:50,700
Oh, you're the guy from before…

129
00:07:51,617 --> 00:07:52,660
What?

130
00:07:53,369 --> 00:07:56,038
Are you one of Jin Ichijo's
actor buddies or something?

131
00:07:56,122 --> 00:07:57,415
Huh?

132
00:07:57,498 --> 00:08:02,003
I, too, like to set things on fire.

133
00:08:02,753 --> 00:08:03,963
What?

134
00:08:07,174 --> 00:08:08,676
Hot, that's hot!

135
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:10,428
So hot! It's burning!

136
00:08:10,511 --> 00:08:12,305
Why? So hot!

137
00:08:12,388 --> 00:08:13,556
Why?

138
00:08:13,639 --> 00:08:14,473
So hot!

139
00:08:14,557 --> 00:08:16,225
-Is it on fire?
-So hot!

140
00:08:16,309 --> 00:08:18,394
-So hot!
-Well then, let's put it out.

141
00:08:22,898 --> 00:08:24,525
Nice underhand throw!

142
00:08:24,609 --> 00:08:26,652
Wait, no. Bad, that's bad.

143
00:08:27,737 --> 00:08:30,531
What did you do?

144
00:08:30,615 --> 00:08:31,866
Why did you throw it?

145
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:33,409
Why did you throw my camera?

146
00:08:33,492 --> 00:08:36,245
Who the hell are you working for?

147
00:08:36,329 --> 00:08:37,705
Just what are you?

148
00:08:38,414 --> 00:08:41,667
I'm the same breed as you guys.

149
00:08:48,382 --> 00:08:49,550
Oh, it's so cute!

150
00:08:49,634 --> 00:08:51,093
You're like an idol.

151
00:08:51,761 --> 00:08:53,679
Where did you buy this, ma'am?

152
00:08:53,763 --> 00:08:55,681
-I want one too.
-Go on!

153
00:08:55,765 --> 00:08:57,892
Did you rummage through my bag?

154
00:08:57,975 --> 00:09:00,311
This is yours, isn't it, ma'am?

155
00:09:01,562 --> 00:09:03,564
No! Um…

156
00:09:03,648 --> 00:09:04,649
Was it in there?

157
00:09:04,732 --> 00:09:07,985
No, I have no intention of using it.

158
00:09:08,069 --> 00:09:09,987
It's just, you know, just in case…

159
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:15,201
You never know what might happen, right?

160
00:09:15,284 --> 00:09:17,703
What do you mean "just in case"?
What case?

161
00:09:17,787 --> 00:09:20,414
-By just in case, I mean…
-There's other stuff too!

162
00:09:20,498 --> 00:09:23,501
-Stop it!
-Stop it! Don't look!

163
00:09:24,585 --> 00:09:25,586
This…

164
00:09:26,379 --> 00:09:28,255
Wait, so those photos…

165
00:09:28,839 --> 00:09:31,050
<i>They were all you, ma'am?</i>

166
00:09:31,634 --> 00:09:33,844
Seriously?

167
00:09:34,428 --> 00:09:36,597
No! Stop it!

168
00:09:36,681 --> 00:09:38,641
We're busted!

169
00:09:38,724 --> 00:09:40,142
Stop it!

170
00:09:40,685 --> 00:09:44,814
-Ryoko!
-Darling!

171
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:48,359
<i>Ryoko!</i>

172
00:09:48,442 --> 00:09:50,152
<i>Yes!</i>

173
00:09:50,236 --> 00:09:52,196
<i>What do you like?</i>

174
00:09:52,279 --> 00:09:54,240
<i>Chocolate mint, but more than that…</i>

175
00:09:54,323 --> 00:09:55,783
<i>I like you!</i>

176
00:10:02,248 --> 00:10:04,417
T-This means…

177
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,001
To spice up their marriage,

178
00:10:06,085 --> 00:10:10,131
the wife dressed up and role-played
as different types of women.

179
00:10:10,214 --> 00:10:13,008
And they were
going on dates out in the city?

180
00:10:13,092 --> 00:10:14,677
Then they got photographed?

181
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,971
Then you should just tell everyone that!

182
00:10:17,054 --> 00:10:20,015
You weren't cheating with several women,
it was all your wife!

183
00:10:20,808 --> 00:10:22,268
How could I possibly say that?

184
00:10:22,852 --> 00:10:24,478
Making my wife, at this age,

185
00:10:24,562 --> 00:10:28,107
do all kinds of cosplay
and wander around the city…

186
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:32,737
If her parents or our relatives
found out about that, we…

187
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:36,031
we would both die of embarrassment!

188
00:10:36,115 --> 00:10:38,576
That's one "we" too many, darling.

189
00:10:38,659 --> 00:10:40,077
That's not true at all!

190
00:10:40,911 --> 00:10:42,538
It's a wonderful thing!

191
00:10:42,621 --> 00:10:44,081
You two want to date

192
00:10:44,165 --> 00:10:46,959
while keeping things fresh,
just like when you were young.

193
00:10:47,042 --> 00:10:49,545
That means you're putting effort
into your marriage!

194
00:10:49,628 --> 00:10:51,714
That's right, it's lovely!

195
00:10:51,797 --> 00:10:54,884
That is what true love is.
You're the ideal couple!

196
00:10:54,967 --> 00:10:57,136
If you can liven things up
with idol cosplay,

197
00:10:57,219 --> 00:10:58,512
do it as much as you want!

198
00:10:58,596 --> 00:11:01,432
Jin, let's announce this to the world.

199
00:11:02,349 --> 00:11:04,185
Prove to your sponsors
and the film industry

200
00:11:04,268 --> 00:11:06,353
that you weren't four-timing anyone!

201
00:11:06,937 --> 00:11:07,772
Okay.

202
00:11:07,855 --> 00:11:09,523
What a great couple!

203
00:11:09,607 --> 00:11:11,609
-What are you doing?
-You look great together.

204
00:11:11,692 --> 00:11:16,071
Mr. Jin, ma'am,
let's tell everyone the truth.

205
00:11:17,448 --> 00:11:18,782
Everyone?

206
00:11:31,003 --> 00:11:32,254
What is it?

207
00:11:32,963 --> 00:11:36,258
What the hell do you want?

208
00:11:36,342 --> 00:11:38,427
No!

209
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,640
Hold on!

210
00:11:47,228 --> 00:11:50,856
Hey! Hold on! Help me!

211
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,442
It's better than going to hell, right?

212
00:11:53,526 --> 00:11:55,194
Come on!

213
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:58,113
Help me! Wait!

214
00:11:58,197 --> 00:11:59,698
Help!

215
00:11:59,782 --> 00:12:01,242
No!

216
00:12:01,325 --> 00:12:05,037
Help me! Hey! Wait!

217
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:07,831
Hey! Come back!

218
00:12:15,631 --> 00:12:18,342
I guess I should report this
to the higher-ups.

219
00:12:25,015 --> 00:12:27,434
I've got this, calm down.

220
00:12:27,935 --> 00:12:29,061
<i>Like this?</i>

221
00:12:29,144 --> 00:12:30,437
<i>Is it rolling already?</i>

222
00:12:30,521 --> 00:12:32,147
<i>It has started.</i>

223
00:12:32,231 --> 00:12:34,024
<i>Well, um…</i>

224
00:12:34,692 --> 00:12:39,238
<i>regarding the recent incident</i>
<i>that's causing a stir,</i>

225
00:12:39,321 --> 00:12:42,825
<i>I, Jin Ichijo, and my wife,</i>
<i>would like to talk about it.</i>

226
00:12:44,827 --> 00:12:47,246
<i>I am so sorry that my husband</i>

227
00:12:47,955 --> 00:12:53,877
<i>was suspected of cheating,</i>
<i>and it caused quite a ruckus.</i>

228
00:12:54,587 --> 00:12:58,173
<i>You see, the truth is,</i>

229
00:12:58,966 --> 00:13:02,678
<i>all of those women were me.</i>

230
00:13:03,512 --> 00:13:08,726
I asked my wife to do cosplay,

231
00:13:08,809 --> 00:13:13,814
and we went out on dates together.

232
00:13:13,897 --> 00:13:17,234
So, this wasn't an affair.

233
00:13:17,318 --> 00:13:19,194
<i>We are husband and wife.</i>

234
00:13:19,278 --> 00:13:21,947
<i>-Yes. We're very sorry.</i>
<i>-We're very sorry.</i>

235
00:13:22,031 --> 00:13:24,158
<i>We apologize for the commotion.</i>

236
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:27,578
Now, this is the correct way
to use the Internet!

237
00:13:27,661 --> 00:13:29,622
Everyone is being so supportive!

238
00:13:29,705 --> 00:13:31,957
Oh, we just got a Super Chat.

239
00:13:32,666 --> 00:13:33,751
Look.

240
00:13:33,834 --> 00:13:36,211
They're saying,
"You're a wonderful couple."

241
00:13:36,295 --> 00:13:37,880
"Sorry for the misunderstanding."

242
00:13:37,963 --> 00:13:39,673
Wow, goodness…

243
00:13:39,757 --> 00:13:41,175
I'm so happy.

244
00:13:41,258 --> 00:13:43,636
-How kind. Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

245
00:13:44,303 --> 00:13:48,891
<i>And, this broadcast was brought to you</i>
<i>by the next big thing, Konta Hoshino!</i>

246
00:13:48,974 --> 00:13:50,309
<i>The light is too close!</i>

247
00:13:50,392 --> 00:13:52,686
<i>Brought to you by…</i>

248
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:54,313
<i>-Hey now!</i>
<i>-I'm sorry!</i>

249
00:13:55,814 --> 00:13:57,024
<i>Too close!</i>

250
00:13:58,567 --> 00:14:00,444
<i>You're in the shot.</i>

251
00:14:01,570 --> 00:14:02,946
<i>How lovely.</i>

252
00:14:03,864 --> 00:14:05,574
They're a great couple, aren't they?

253
00:14:05,658 --> 00:14:07,826
Even if they go a bit overboard.

254
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:09,328
Going overboard is fine.

255
00:14:09,411 --> 00:14:11,038
I want to get married too.

256
00:14:11,121 --> 00:14:16,960
Get married and be a lovey-dovey
couple forever, just like them!

257
00:14:17,044 --> 00:14:18,045
Exactly.

258
00:14:18,128 --> 00:14:22,132
We're on a hard-earned vacation,
so we've got to find some romance.

259
00:14:23,926 --> 00:14:28,806
We can't just be drinking stupid booze
and getting wasted every time.

260
00:14:28,889 --> 00:14:30,516
Romance, huh.

261
00:14:30,599 --> 00:14:33,102
Midori, you seriously
need to get a boyfriend soon!

262
00:14:33,185 --> 00:14:36,313
Not having dated a guy at your age
is honestly a red flag!

263
00:14:36,397 --> 00:14:39,733
Let's invite some guys over
and have a mixer at this villa!

264
00:14:39,817 --> 00:14:40,651
What?

265
00:14:41,235 --> 00:14:42,778
A mixer at the villa…

266
00:14:42,861 --> 00:14:44,530
That sounds just like
a reality show. I love it.

267
00:14:44,613 --> 00:14:45,614
A reality show?

268
00:14:45,698 --> 00:14:47,074
Like a dating show?

269
00:14:47,157 --> 00:14:48,867
I hate that, no way!

270
00:14:48,951 --> 00:14:50,536
-No.
-But, wait…

271
00:14:53,914 --> 00:14:56,583
<i>Mr. Nishigami. I wonder where he went.</i>

272
00:15:21,442 --> 00:15:24,653
<i>I wonder if I'm even capable</i>
<i>of falling in love.</i>

273
00:15:51,513 --> 00:15:52,431
So today is…

274
00:15:53,557 --> 00:15:55,434
Yes! It’s a girls' day.

275
00:15:55,517 --> 00:15:58,312
-Well then…
-Oh, wait…

276
00:15:58,395 --> 00:16:01,982
I wonder where everyone meets
their soulmates.

277
00:16:02,066 --> 00:16:04,443
The new season of <i>Last Princess</i>
is streaming!

278
00:16:04,526 --> 00:16:06,111
All right, let’s watch it! Right now!

279
00:16:06,195 --> 00:16:08,906
I'm in the mood for romance,
so we are watching this now!

280
00:16:09,490 --> 00:16:10,866
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

281
00:16:10,949 --> 00:16:12,701
This guy seems super shady.

282
00:16:12,785 --> 00:16:14,411
I'm 27 years old.

283
00:16:14,495 --> 00:16:15,746
I'm a cheerleader.

284
00:16:15,829 --> 00:16:17,247
I'm attending a training school.

285
00:16:17,331 --> 00:16:18,540
It’s clout chasing.

286
00:16:18,624 --> 00:16:20,167
I bet it's scripted.

287
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:23,045
Midori! If you talk like that,
you can't enjoy dating shows!

288
00:16:23,128 --> 00:16:24,296
Excuse me.

289
00:16:24,379 --> 00:16:26,006
Who are you?

290
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:27,549
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

